---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";

const lastUpdated = "September 27, 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Terms & Conditions — VarianceCalc"
  description="Terms and conditions for using VarianceCalc, a free browser-based variance and standard deviation calculator."
  skipTo="main-content"
>
  <SiteHeader currentPath="/terms" />

  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="border-b border-hairline">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pt-16 pb-12 sm:px-6 sm:pt-20">
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink sm:text-5xl">
          Terms &amp; Conditions
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-mute">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="border-b border-hairline">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-8 px-5 py-14 text-base leading-relaxed text-body sm:px-6 sm:py-16">
        <p>
          By using VarianceCalc ("the site", "this tool"), you agree to the following
          terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the site.
        </p>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Use of the service</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            VarianceCalc is provided free of charge for personal, educational, and
            professional use. You may use it to calculate variance, standard deviation,
            and related statistics on data you provide. You agree not to misuse the
            service, including attempting to disrupt its operation, reverse-engineer it
            for malicious purposes, or use it in a manner that violates applicable law.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">No warranty</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The calculator is provided "as is" and "as available," without warranties of
            any kind, express or implied, including but not limited to accuracy,
            reliability, or fitness for a particular purpose. While we've built and tested
            the underlying statistics engine carefully, VarianceCalc is a general-purpose
            tool and should not be the sole basis for medical, financial, legal, safety,
            or other high-stakes decisions. Always verify results that matter using a
            second method or professional judgment.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Limitation of liability</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            To the fullest extent permitted by law, VarianceCalc and its operators are not
            liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, or consequential damages arising
            from your use of, or inability to use, this site or its calculations.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Your data</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            All calculations run locally in your browser; we do not receive or store the
            data you enter. See our
            <a href="/privacy-policy" class="text-link hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a>
            for details. You are solely responsible for the data you choose to input and
            for any link you generate and share using the "Copy link" feature.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Intellectual property</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The design, branding, and code of VarianceCalc belong to their respective
            owners. You may not copy, redistribute, or resell the site or its source as
            your own product without permission.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Changes to the service or terms</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We may update, modify, or discontinue features of the site at any time, and
            may revise these terms as needed. Continued use of the site after changes are
            posted constitutes acceptance of the updated terms.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Contact</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Questions about these terms? Visit our
            <a href="/contact" class="text-link hover:underline">Contact Us</a> page.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
</Layout>
